    "turn_text": "I guess, so I agree with the long term. I do believe we need this course correction. You can look at NAFTA. You can look at China's entry in the World Trade Organization. And you can see how that one push manufacturers overseas, particularly to Mexico with NAFTA. And then with China's entry in the World Trade Organization, there's just this influx of cheap goods. So I agree with the long term outlook on it and the course correction. Will there be short-term pain? And what does that short-term pain mean for us in the midterms? Obviously, we saw these races last night. Fortunately, Republicans held on to the two House seats in the special elections. But we lost the Wisconsin Supreme Court race by 10, and those margins in the House races were much less than we saw in prior elections. So I mean, what does that all mean, I guess, for, you know, and then we're not going to have President Trump's in office, but we're not going to have him on the ballot driving turnout. So I guess what does this all sort of collectively mean for the Republican Party moving forward, particularly looking ahead at the midterms?",
